    gmeow:useWhen "Use for a source-reported wish to play."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid inferring a play demand from restlessness or assuming a game was started."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the Desire’s stated Goal and any supplied play context independently."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The open response vocabulary imposes no matching play response or guaranteed satisfaction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "Record the play wish: ex:playWish gmeow:demandKind gmeow:demandKindPlay ."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:demandResponseCuddle
    a gmeow:DemandResponse ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agency-records> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "cuddle response"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The source reports cuddling as the answering interaction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the actual answering occurrence is reported as cuddling."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid deriving cuddling merely from a cuddles demand or an affectionate mood."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Select on the answering Event and use answersDemand for its exact addressed Desire."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "A reported cuddle neither proves enjoyment nor completes a GoalEvaluation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "Classify the cuddle answer: ex:cuddleAnswer gmeow:demandResponse gmeow:demandResponseCuddle ."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:demandResponseLap
    a gmeow:DemandResponse ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agency-records> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "lap response"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The source reports that a lap was offered as the answering interaction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the source explicitly records a lap being given or offered in response."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid interpreting a response label as actual relocation, a body or acceptance of the offer."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Keep the offer occurrence distinct from the wanted lap and any later resting occurrence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The source’s simulated or physical interaction convention remains explicit rather than universal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "Classify the lap answer: ex:lapAnswer gmeow:demandResponse gmeow:demandResponseLap ."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:demandResponsePet
    a gmeow:DemandResponse ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agency-records> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "petting response"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The source reports petting or affectionate stroking as the answering interaction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for a source-recorded petting response to an identified Desire."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid reading pet as an animal acquired or assuming a petting request was satisfied."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the actual response occurrence and its attribution separately from contact evidence and judgment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "No permission, affective improvement or accepted fulfillment follows from this kind alone."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "Classify the petting answer: ex:petAnswer gmeow:demandResponse gmeow:demandResponsePet ."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:eventTypeCreatureGenesis
    a gmeow:EventType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agency-records> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "creature genesis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The source reports that a creature came into being within its stated environment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for an explicitly reported origin occurrence of the represented creature."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid inferring biological birth, a new software process or an actual-world organism from genesis wording."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Classify the occurrence through eventType; retain the source’s creature identity and provider-world scope."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "A simulated origin remains scoped to its source environment; it does not generate an entity or initialize a runtime."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "Classify the reported origin: ex:genesis gmeow:eventType gmeow:eventTypeCreatureGenesis ."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:eventTypeCreatureRenamed
    a gmeow:EventType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agency-records> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "creature renamed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The source reports a change of a creature’s name while retaining that creature’s identity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the source identifies a renaming occurrence rather than a newly created creature."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid merging creatures with matching names or deleting an older name claim."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the exact old and new source names with their own validity and displayability evidence when supplied."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "This is not the organization-specific eventTypeRename and supplies no universal name resolver."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "Classify the name change: ex:renaming gmeow:eventType gmeow:eventTypeCreatureRenamed ."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:eventTypeCreatureTransition
    a gmeow:EventType ;
